isn't it, you know?

263
00:11:42,994 --> 00:11:47,957
Just the four us,
just hanging.

264
00:11:47,999 --> 00:11:49,417
Dude, are you okay?

265
00:11:49,459 --> 00:11:51,169
And when are the fajitas
going to be ready?

266
00:11:52,504 --> 00:11:54,506
I'm fine, okay?

267
00:11:54,548 --> 00:11:55,756
I'm great.

268
00:11:55,798 --> 00:11:59,469
I'm just, I'm just
proud of us, you know?

269
00:11:59,511 --> 00:12:02,430
There's no weirdness,
no tension.

270
00:12:02,472 --> 00:12:05,684
No awareness.

271
00:12:05,724 --> 00:12:07,352
You know, we make
a great foursome.

272
00:12:07,394 --> 00:12:08,769
We should do more
stuff together.

273
00:12:08,811 --> 00:12:09,979
( gasps )

274
00:12:10,021 --> 00:12:11,606
Let's take a trip.

275
00:12:12,607 --> 00:12:14,192
Okay, where
do you think

276
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:15,694
we-we can go?

277
00:12:15,734 --> 00:12:17,278
( dinging )
My fajitas!

278
00:12:20,657 --> 00:12:22,617
Look, Charlie.

279
00:12:22,659 --> 00:12:24,244
I just want you to know,

280
00:12:24,285 --> 00:12:26,162
Ross is just having
a little trouble

281
00:12:26,204 --> 00:12:28,665
adjusting to the thought
of Joey and me.

282
00:12:28,707 --> 00:12:31,084
You know, he normally
doesn't drink like this.

283
00:12:31,125 --> 00:12:32,793
Oh, you know what,
this is nothing.

284
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,546
My father is a raging alcoholic.

285
00:12:38,091 --> 00:12:39,342
Oh, I'm sorry.

286
00:12:39,384 --> 00:12:40,968
Have I made this evening
uncomfortable?

287
00:12:43,471 --> 00:12:44,805
Fajitas!

288
00:12:44,847 --> 00:12:47,475
Be careful, very hot plate.
Very hot.

289
00:12:47,517 --> 00:12:49,644
Ross, you don't even
have oven mitts on.

290
00:12:49,686 --> 00:12:52,063
( chuckles )

291
00:12:52,105 --> 00:12:56,025
That is going to hurt tomorrow.

292
00:12:59,112 --> 00:13:00,530
Okay, well,
this is crazy.

293
00:13:00,572 --> 00:13:02,073
We can't seriously be talking

294
00:13:02,115 --> 00:13:04,200
about me taking
one of your kids, can we?

295
00:13:04,242 --> 00:13:05,744
Oh, no, of course we're not.

296
00:13:05,784 --> 00:13:06,745
It's insane.

297
00:13:06,785 --> 00:13:07,954
I know.

298
00:13:07,995 --> 00:13:09,414
Alice would never go for it,
right?

299
00:13:09,456 --> 00:13:11,249
I don't know.
She's pretty tired, too.

300
00:13:11,291 --> 00:13:12,833
I think we could get her
on board.

301
00:13:14,210 --> 00:13:17,297
Well, just, you know,
for argument's sake,

302
00:13:17,338 --> 00:13:18,757
you know, hypothetically,

303
00:13:18,797 --> 00:13:21,134
which one would you
be willing to give up?

304
00:13:21,175 --> 00:13:22,927
Huh...

305
00:13:22,969 --> 00:13:24,929
Frank Junior Jr.

306
00:13:24,971 --> 00:13:27,432
Uh, you'd be getting
a really good one.

307
00:13:27,474 --> 00:13:29,808
I mean,
you know, he's really funny.

308
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:33,605
Like, the other day,
he made up this joke.

309
00:13:33,647 --> 00:13:37,734
What's green and says,
"Hey, I'm a frog"?

310
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:41,780
( laughs ):
A talking frog.

311
00:13:44,115 --> 00:13:47,285
Oh, no, you can't have him.
He's too funny.

312
00:13:47,327 --> 00:13:49,036
Well, all right, that's fine.

313
00:13:49,078 --> 00:13:50,455
What about, um, Leslie?

314
00:13:50,497 --> 00:13:52,707
Oh, no, no, not Leslie, no.

315
00:13:52,749 --> 00:13:57,295
She's, she's the only one that
knows how to burp the alphabet.

316
00:13:57,337 --> 00:13:59,756
All right,
so that leaves Chandler.

317
00:13:59,798 --> 00:14:01,132
Oh, no, you
can't have Chandler.

318
00:14:01,174 --> 00:14:02,216
No, no, no, no.

319
00:14:02,258 --> 00:14:03,134
She's my little
genius.

320
00:14:03,176 --> 00:14:05,428
I got big hopes for her.

321
00:14:05,470 --> 00:14:09,599
She's going to be a doctor
or... Realtor.

322
00:14:11,434 --> 00:14:15,522
Wow, Frank, I think
we just ran out of kids.

323
00:14:15,563 --> 00:14:18,525
Oh, I think you're right.

324
00:14:21,319 --> 00:14:22,862
Oh, wow.

325
00:14:22,903 --> 00:14:25,615
Phoebe, I don't think
I can give one of them up.

326
00:14:25,657 --> 00:14:27,867
I mean, you know,
they drive me crazy,

327
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:30,077
but they're my babies.

328
00:14:32,455 --> 00:14:35,500
I'm sorry, Frank, I didn't
realize things were so bad.

329
00:14:35,542 --> 00:14:37,585
You know, I'll help out more.

330
00:14:37,627 --> 00:14:39,253
I can baby-sit
any time you want.

331
00:14:39,295 --> 00:14:41,047
You name the day
and I'll be there.

332
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,006
How 'bout tomorrow?

333
00:14:42,048 --> 00:14:43,924
Well, that's not good.

334
00:14:43,966 --> 00:14:45,468
But,
you know,

335
00:14:45,510 --> 00:14:47,970
I can move some stuff around
and I'll be there.

336
00:14:48,012 --> 00:14:50,097
You and Alice just take
the whole day together.

337
00:14:50,139 --> 00:14:52,350
You'd do that for us?

338
00:14:52,392 --> 00:14:54,811
Are you kidding?
That's what sisters are for.

339
00:14:56,312 --> 00:14:57,689
Oh...

340
00:15:00,650 --> 00:15:03,319
Oh, look at them.

341
00:15:03,361 --> 00:15:06,364
I love you
so much.

342
00:15:07,657 --> 00:15:10,034
Oh, crap, don't wake up.
Don't wake up.

343
00:15:13,621 --> 00:15:15,039
Where are Bill
and Colleen?

344
00:15:15,081 --> 00:15:16,875
They're in the kitchen
getting us something to eat.

345
00:15:16,915 --> 00:15:18,585
Can you believe
how nice they are?

346
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:20,086
We have to leave.

347
00:15:21,838 --> 00:15:24,674
Why?
What did you do in the bathroom?

348
00:15:24,716 --> 00:15:26,050
I didn't get
to the bathroom.

349
00:15:26,092 --> 00:15:27,510
I bumped into Owen
on the way,

350
00:15:27,552 --> 00:15:29,178
and he didn't know
he was adopted.

351
00:15:29,220 --> 00:15:32,056
And there's a slight chance
I may have told him.

352
00:15:32,098 --> 00:15:33,725
Oh, my God.
Where's my purse?

353
00:15:33,767 --> 00:15:36,018
No, you know what, I can
replace everything in there.

354
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,270
Get that binder and let's go.

355
00:15:37,311 --> 00:15:38,396
Hey.

356
00:15:38,438 --> 00:15:40,022
BILL:
Some little snacks

357
00:15:40,064 --> 00:15:41,232
for everybody.

358
00:15:41,274 --> 00:15:43,234
Oh, you don't have
to eat the sour worms.

359
00:15:43,276 --> 00:15:44,485
Those are for Owen.

360
00:15:44,527 --> 00:15:46,362
COLLEEN:
I'll go get him
in a second.

361
00:15:46,404 --> 00:15:47,822
By the way,
you should know,

362
00:15:47,864 --> 00:15:49,866
we haven't told him
he's adopted yet.

363
00:15:49,908 --> 00:15:52,201
But kids are so intuitive.

364
00:15:52,243 --> 00:15:55,246
Don't you think on some
level he already knows?

365
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:56,706
I'm adopted?!

366
00:15:56,748 --> 00:15:59,125
See, intuitive.

367
00:15:59,166 --> 00:16:00,209
What?

368
00:16:00,251 --> 00:16:01,377
Where did you
hear that?

369
00:16:01,419 --> 00:16:02,629
He told me.

370
00:16:04,130 --> 00:16:08,259
And he paid me $50
not to tell.

371
00:16:08,301 --> 00:16:11,095
Which technically now
you should give back.

372
00:16:13,431 --> 00:16:16,016
You told him he's adopted?

373
00:16:16,058 --> 00:16:17,602
I'm so sorry,
but you should have

374
00:16:17,644 --> 00:16:19,019
a sign out there
or something.

375
00:16:19,061 --> 00:16:20,605
Or at least whisper
it to people

376
00:16:20,647 --> 00:16:22,482
when they
come in the door.

377
00:16:22,523 --> 00:16:24,233
( whispering ):
Owen doesn't know
he's adopted.

378
00:16:24,275 --> 00:16:25,902
And he also thinks
Santa is real.

379
00:16:25,944 --> 00:16:27,904
He isn't?

380
00:16:29,071 --> 00:16:31,365
We have to get out
of here, baby.

381
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:37,956
Everyone, I would like
to make a toast.

382
00:16:37,997 --> 00:16:41,083
To Rachel and Joey.

383
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,460
Oy.

384
00:16:42,502 --> 00:16:44,044
And...

385
00:16:44,086 --> 00:16:46,130
to love.

386
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:50,176
Ah, love.

387
00:16:52,094 --> 00:16:54,806
L-O-V-E, love.

388
00:16:54,848 --> 00:16:57,099
"L" is for life.

389
00:16:57,141 --> 00:16:59,602
And what is life
without love?

390
00:17:00,812 --> 00:17:02,271
Oh, my God.
Are we supposed to answer?

391
00:17:04,524 --> 00:17:08,611
"O" is for...

392
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:11,113
"Oh, wow."

393
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:21,332
The "V" is for this very
surprising turn of events.

394
00:17:21,374 --> 00:17:25,712
Which I am still fine with,
by the way.

395
00:17:27,380 --> 00:17:28,464
( screeching ):
"E..."

396
00:17:32,343 --> 00:17:38,391
is for how extremely normal
I find it

397
00:17:38,432 --> 00:17:41,519
that you two...

398
00:17:41,561 --> 00:17:43,062
are together.

399
00:17:45,648 --> 00:17:48,401
And that one day
you might get married.

400
00:17:50,570 --> 00:17:54,574
And have children of your own.

401
00:17:57,744 --> 00:17:59,203
Dude, are you okay?

402
00:17:59,245 --> 00:18:01,163
Totally.

403
00:18:02,999 --> 00:18:04,625
Ross, you don't seem okay.

404
00:18:04,667 --> 00:18:08,421
I'm sorry. It must be
the pressure of entertaining.

405
00:18:11,340 --> 00:18:15,720
I think everyone would feel
better if we had some flan.

406
00:18:15,762 --> 00:18:16,971
Wait, Ross.

407
00:18:17,013 --> 00:18:19,223
Ross, I, um, I have to take off.

408
00:18:19,265 --> 00:18:21,225
No.
I'm sorry.

409
00:18:21,267 --> 00:18:24,020
I have a really early
class in the morning.

410
00:18:24,062 --> 00:18:27,607
This has been lovely.

411
00:18:27,648 --> 00:18:29,358
Wasn't it?

412
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:32,403
And you thought it would
be awkward with Joey,

413
00:18:32,445 --> 00:18:34,948
and that you never
really liked Rachel.

414
00:18:36,156 --> 00:18:38,743
You are on fire.

415
00:18:38,785 --> 00:18:40,078
I'll call you
in the morning, okay?

416
00:18:40,119 --> 00:18:41,370
Okay.
All right.

417
00:18:45,541 --> 00:18:47,460
Oh, God, Rachel, what Ross
just said, this is just...

418
00:18:47,501 --> 00:18:50,797
Oh, that's okay.
Girls tend not to like me.

419
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:51,881
Bye.

420
00:18:54,717 --> 00:18:58,596
Okay, I guess
it's just flan for three.

421
00:18:58,638 --> 00:19:03,101
Hey... hey, that rhymes.

422
00:19:04,727 --> 00:19:06,104
You know what, Ross?

423
00:19:06,145 --> 00:19:08,022
I think we're going
to take off, too.

424
00:19:08,064 --> 00:19:09,398
Oh, oh...

425
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:10,775
of course.

426
00:19:10,817 --> 00:19:13,027
God, I'm so stupid.

427
00:19:13,069 --> 00:19:14,946
You guys are a couple now.

428
00:19:14,988 --> 00:19:17,448
I mean, you probably
just want to be alone.

429
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:19,283
No, no, it's just
it's getting late...

430
00:19:19,325 --> 00:19:20,743
Hey, hey, hey.
It's fine.

431
00:19:20,785 --> 00:19:21,911
It's totally fine.

432
00:19:21,953 --> 00:19:23,079
I've got plenty of margaritas.

433
00:19:23,121 --> 00:19:24,956
It's all good.

434
00:19:24,998 --> 00:19:26,290
( dinging )

435
00:19:30,795 --> 00:19:33,714
I don't even know
what that's for.

436
00:19:38,719 --> 00:19:39,887
You know what?

437
00:19:39,929 --> 00:19:41,973
I think I'm going
to stay here

438
00:19:42,015 --> 00:19:43,808
and make sure he's okay.

439
00:19:43,850 --> 00:19:45,476
Yeah, that's probably
a good idea.

440
00:19:45,518 --> 00:19:46,769
Just, I'll see you
in the morning.

441
00:19:46,811 --> 00:19:47,812
Uh-huh. Okay.

442
00:19:49,229 --> 00:19:50,857
Hey, you know, Joey,

443
00:19:50,898 --> 00:19:54,819
I don't think he's ever
going to be okay with this.

444
00:19:54,861 --> 00:19:56,863
Doesn't look good, does it?

445
00:20:17,216 --> 00:20:18,676
JOEY:
Morning.

446
00:20:18,718 --> 00:20:20,011
Here you go.

447
00:20:20,053 --> 00:20:21,303
Thanks.

448
00:20:21,345 --> 00:20:24,098
Did you, you stay
here all night?

449
00:20:24,140 --> 00:20:25,641
Yeah.

450
00:20:27,060 --> 00:20:30,270
So you took off
my pants and shoes?

451
00:20:30,312 --> 00:20:32,023
No, no, no, no.

452
00:20:32,065 --> 00:20:33,774
You actually did that

453
00:20:33,816 --> 00:20:36,402
when you were dancing
to the Chicago soundtrack.

454
00:20:38,236 --> 00:20:42,950
Look, uh, Ross, about,
about Rachel and I.

455
00:20:42,992 --> 00:20:45,411
Listen, you don't have
to worry about that, okay,

456
00:20:45,452 --> 00:20:47,705
because nothing's going
to happen.

457
00:20:47,747 --> 00:20:49,123
What do you mean?

458
00:20:50,833 --> 00:20:52,459
Well, she and I said
from the beginning

459
00:20:52,501 --> 00:20:53,836
that we weren't
going to do anything

460
00:20:53,878 --> 00:20:55,213
unless you were okay with it.

461
00:20:55,254 --> 00:20:57,215
And clearly...

462
00:20:57,255 --> 00:21:00,134
What are you talking about?
I'm fine.

463
00:21:00,176 --> 00:21:02,136
It's okay, Ross.

464
00:21:02,178 --> 00:21:04,471
You know, I, I totally
understand.

465
00:21:04,513 --> 00:21:06,348
Of course you're
not fine.

466
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:08,392
You're...

467
00:21:08,434 --> 00:21:10,895
You're Ross and Rachel.

468
00:21:12,605 --> 00:21:15,024
Yeah, except we're not.

469
00:21:15,066 --> 00:21:20,738
I mean, we haven't been
a couple in, like...

470
00:21:20,780 --> 00:21:23,407
six years.

471
00:21:23,449 --> 00:21:26,827
Oh, my God,
is that right?

472
00:21:26,869 --> 00:21:30,039
Has it been that long?

473
00:21:30,081 --> 00:21:32,875
That's what I hear, yeah.

474
00:21:34,376 --> 00:21:36,129
This is crazy.

475
00:21:36,170 --> 00:21:39,257
I mean, six years,
and because of me

476
00:21:39,298 --> 00:21:43,302
you guys aren't
going to be together?

477
00:21:43,343 --> 00:21:44,762
Can I ask you
something?

478
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:47,431
Really, what...

479
00:21:47,473 --> 00:21:50,476
what is this thing
with you and Rachel?

480
00:21:52,228 --> 00:21:54,188
Come on, I mean,
you know me.

481
00:21:54,230 --> 00:21:55,940
( chuckling ):
You know...

482
00:21:55,982 --> 00:21:58,692
Joey.

483
00:22:05,241 --> 00:22:07,285
I'm crazy about her.

484
00:22:12,999 --> 00:22:16,085
And she feels
the same way?

485
00:22:17,336 --> 00:22:19,880
I think so.

486
00:22:21,882 --> 00:22:25,970
Well, then, maybe it's
time we all moved on.

487
00:22:26,012 --> 00:22:29,140
Yeah, but, Ross, I mean,
you're not okay with it.

488
00:22:29,182 --> 00:22:32,226
No, but...
I want to be.

489
00:22:32,268 --> 00:22:36,314
And, hey, I will be.

490
00:22:39,775 --> 00:22:41,610
Besides, I'm with
Charlie, right?

491
00:22:41,652 --> 00:22:43,403
Oh, my God.

492
00:22:43,445 --> 00:22:44,864
I'm still with Charlie,
aren't I?

493
00:22:44,905 --> 00:22:46,490
I mean, she didn't see
the dance, did she?

494
00:22:46,532 --> 00:22:47,741
No, no, no.

495
00:22:47,783 --> 00:22:52,370
No, that was, uh,
that was just for me.

496
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:59,837
Are you, uh,
are you sure about this?

497
00:22:59,879 --> 00:23:02,715
Yeah, I'm sure.

498
00:23:04,925 --> 00:23:09,263
And... we're okay?

499
00:23:09,305 --> 00:23:10,848
( chuckles )

500
00:23:12,516 --> 00:23:14,768
( gasps )

501
00:23:21,317 --> 00:23:22,526
Hey, Pheebs,

502
00:23:22,568 --> 00:23:23,777
um, we just want to
give you a heads-up.

503
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,906
Bill and Colleen hate us.

504
00:23:26,947 --> 00:23:28,406
Owen didn't know
he was adopted

505
00:23:28,448 --> 00:23:29,449
and Monica told him.

506
00:23:29,491 --> 00:23:31,077
What?

507
00:23:31,118 --> 00:23:33,162
Still, he had
to find out sometime.

508
00:23:33,204 --> 00:23:34,747
Yeah, but how would
you like it

509
00:23:34,788 --> 00:23:36,498
if someone told the triplets
that you gave birth to them?

510
00:23:42,213 --> 00:23:44,382
I'm going to go tell Emma
she was an accident.

511
00:23:46,550 --> 00:23:51,138
Captioned by
Media Access Group at WGBH
access.wgbh.org

